# TypeScript standards

- Keep strict mode enabled; do not use `any` or unchecked casts.
- Parse external input with Zod and derive types from schemas.
- Keep qualification functions pure and integrations behind interfaces.
- Use explicit result states for expected failures; never swallow errors.
- Preserve missing business data as `null`, not zero or fabricated defaults.
